summary:
  The exit-handler clear of the in-flight guard is gone — titles freeze for
  the playing station.

history:
  The flag exists because two overlapping reader.py runs raced and the slower
  one overwrote the newer title. It has two clear sites (measured 2026-08-09:
  main.qml 8443 in the exit handler, 8515 in onSourceChanged since 2026-07-28,
  so a new station never inherits a raised flag). This mutant drops the exit
  handler's one — the widget asks once and every later query on the SAME
  station is skipped; only switching stations re-arms it. Losing the other
  site instead would be quieter still, which is what makes the pair worth a
  behavioural test rather than a grep.

target:
  package/contents/ui/main.qml

find:
  // exit from this handler.
              root._icyInFlight = false;

replace:
  // exit from this handler.
              // root._icyInFlight = false;

expect:
  A test that issues two title queries in sequence and asserts the second one
  actually goes out. No such test exists yet — this mutant is expected to
  survive until the metadata engine is testable (stage 4 of the plan).
